You are an expert Python and ML engineer. Build a single Python script called
`process_rationalization.py` that analyzes process-to-database relationships
and classifies them using ML-based set similarity techniques.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
INPUT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
JSON file with this exact structure:
{
  "P1": ["db1", "db3", "db4"],
  "P2": ["db1", "db3"],
  "P3": ["db5", "db6"]
}
Each key is a processId, value is list of database names it uses.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
OUTPUT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
output.xlsx with exactly 3 tabs:

TAB 1 — Exact_Match
  Columns: Process_A | Process_B | Common_DBs | Total_DBs | Match_%
  Condition: Jaccard == 1.0 (sets are identical)

TAB 2 — Overlap
  Columns: Process_A | Process_B | Overlap_Type | Common_DBs |
           Only_in_A | Only_in_B | Jaccard_Score | Overlap_%
  Overlap_Type values: "Subset" (one set fully inside other)
                       "Partial" (some common, neither contains other)
  Condition: 0 < Jaccard < 1.0

TAB 3 — Disjoint
  Columns: Process_A | Process_B | DBs_in_A | DBs_in_B | Reason
  Condition: Jaccard == 0 (no common databases)

All DB columns should be pipe-separated strings e.g. "db1|db3|db4"

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ML PIPELINE (non-LLM)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Step 1 — Load & parse JSON into {processId: set(databases)}
Step 2 — Encode using sklearn MultiLabelBinarizer → binary matrix
Step 3 — Compute pairwise Jaccard similarity matrix using scipy
Step 4 — Run DBSCAN on (1 - Jaccard) distance matrix for clustering
Step 5 — Classify every unique pair (Pi, Pj) using this logic:
           if intersection == set_A == set_B  → Exact
           elif intersection == set_A or == set_B → Overlap/Subset
           elif 0 < |intersection| < |union|  → Overlap/Partial
           else                               → Disjoint
Step 6 — Enrich each pair: common_dbs, only_in_A, only_in_B, jaccard, overlap_pct
Step 7 — Write to 3 Excel tabs using openpyxl

